 "events": [
  {
   "tStartMs": 14980,
   "dDurationMs": 1480,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "Hey everyone, Grant here."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 16820,
   "dDurationMs": 3008,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "This is the first video in a series on the essence of calculus,"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 19828,
   "dDurationMs": 3772,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "and I'll be publishing the following videos once per day for the next 10 days."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 24300,
   "dDurationMs": 2611,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "The goal here, as the name suggests, is to really get"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 26911,
   "dDurationMs": 2809,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "the heart of the subject out in one binge-watchable set."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 30320,
   "dDurationMs": 3859,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "But with a topic that's as broad as calculus, there's a lot of things that can mean,"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 34179,
   "dDurationMs": 2021,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "so here's what I have in mind specifically."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 36940,
   "dDurationMs": 2473,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "Calculus has a lot of rules and formulas which"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 39413,
   "dDurationMs": 2527,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "are often presented as things to be memorized."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 42480,
   "dDurationMs": 3274,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "Lots of derivative formulas, the product rule, the chain rule,"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 45754,
   "dDurationMs": 4224,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "implicit differentiation, the fact that integrals and derivatives are opposite,"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 49978,
   "dDurationMs": 2482,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "Taylor series, just a lot of things like that."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 52960,
   "dDurationMs": 2173,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "And my goal is for you to come away feeling like"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 55133,
   "dDurationMs": 1947,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "you could have invented calculus yourself."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 57640,
   "dDurationMs": 3998,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "That is, cover all those core ideas, but in a way that makes clear where they"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 61638,
   "dDurationMs": 4362,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "actually come from, and what they really mean, using an all-around visual approach."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 66920,
   "dDurationMs": 3507,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "Inventing math is no joke, and there is a difference between being"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 70427,
   "dDurationMs": 3613,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "told why something's true, and actually generating it from scratch."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 74680,
   "dDurationMs": 4411,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "But at all points, I want you to think to yourself, if you were an early mathematician,"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tStartMs": 79091,
   "dDurationMs": 2941,
   "segs": [
    {
     "utf8": "pondering these ideas and drawing out the right diagrams,"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "windows": []
}